<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <StartupProject>DevToolbox.UI</StartupProject>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    The version, for every project in the solution. This is the only place it is written down.

    Two numbers come out of these two properties, and they are for different readers:

      AssemblyVersion / FileVersion   0.4.0.0          what MSIX and Windows compare
      InformationalVersion            0.4.0-alpha.1    what a person reads

    MSIX requires exactly four numeric parts and rejects a prerelease suffix, and Windows App
    Installer only upgrades to a numerically *higher* version — so the four-part number must only
    ever go up, and the channel cannot live in it. Hence VersionSuffix: the channel is a name
    carried by InformationalVersion, which is what the status bar and Settings show.

    Build-Installer.ps1 reads both back out of the published executable rather than taking a
    -Version argument, so the package version cannot drift from the assembly's.

      alpha    0.x       the two of us, and the first tester
      beta     0.9.x     the WebTeam subteam
      release  1.x       team, then company

    Any build that leaves this machine must raise the four-part number, so bump the patch in
    VersionPrefix as well as the suffix. Bumping VersionSuffix alone reads like a new build but
    leaves the package at the same 0.4.0.0, and App Installer only upgrades to a numerically higher
    version — it would decline to install over its predecessor, silently, on every machine.
    Promotion to beta is a bar, not a date — see
    [[03-Projects/DevToolbox/Plans/2026-08-18-alpha-launch-feedback]] in the vault.
  -->
  <!--
    Beta, opening the 0.9.x band this file reserves for it. 0.9.0.0 is numerically above the
    0.4.5.0 it replaces, so App Installer upgrades to it rather than declining; and the suffix
    is what AppVersion.ChannelFrom reads, so the status bar and Settings relabel themselves
    without a copy change anywhere.
  -->
  <!--
    0.9.2 / beta.3: the Projects tab's customization layer — smart folder cards that can be
    renamed, merged, relabelled and hidden, with the edits surviving a rescan; the Smart Folders
    dialog reorganised into sections with icon and colour pickers; groups hideable and draggable
    to last.
  -->
  <!--
    0.9.3 / beta.4: arranging is a dialog about one named group rather than a toolbar mode, cards
    can actually be reordered as well as merged, and each group header carries its own sort with a
    remembered Custom option.
  -->
  <!--
    0.9.4 / beta.5: right-click menus on the workspace cards and their location rows, the arrange
    dialog laid out as the group's own card grid instead of a column, and the redundant "Default"
    sort dropped where it was identical to Name A-Z.
  -->
  <!--
    0.9.5 / beta.6: fixes right-clicking a collapsed card's quick-open chip, which gave the card's
    menu instead of the chip's — a regression from the card-level right-click added in 0.9.4.
  -->
  <!--
    0.9.5.1 / beta.7: context menus dismiss on any outside left-click, the +N location badge stays
    on its own row, and the merge-undo button says "Split cards".

    Four parts in VersionPrefix from here, not three. The four-part number only has to *rise*, and
    the last digit is the smallest step that does it — which keeps the patch digit for something
    worth calling a release rather than spending one on every fix. AssemblyVersion and FileVersion
    take VersionPrefix verbatim when it already has four parts, so 0.9.5.1 is what MSIX compares and
    what Build-Installer.ps1 reads back out of the executable.
  -->
  <!--
    0.9.5.2 / beta.8: "Open in VS Code" on the location menus, opening the folder around the
    location rather than the file itself.
  -->
  <!--
    0.9.5.3 / beta.9: a .code-workspace opens as the workspace again, rather than as its containing
    folder. 0.9.5.2 shipped without that exception for about a minute.
  -->
  <!--
    0.9.6 / beta.10: the seasonal overhaul. Easter and Fourth of July are new themes; Winter is a
    deep blue night instead of the one light-grounded season; Fall, Halloween and Thanksgiving grew
    ornament that rests on the footer, and Halloween a cauldron you can stir at the bottom of
    Settings. Fall and Thanksgiving also lost the stutter in their falling leaves, which was a seam
    in one keyframe rather than a performance problem — see css/themeEffects.css.

    The patch digit moves rather than the fourth part, which is what 0.9.5.1 above reserved it for:
    this is the first change in the 0.9.x line big enough to be worth calling a release. Written as
    four parts all the same — 0.9.6.0 — because MSIX compares VersionPrefix verbatim and 0.9.6.0
    rises above 0.9.5.3.
  -->
  <!--
    0.9.7 / beta.11: the Log Viewer's advanced SQL mode can save, group and recall its queries, and
    colours what you type; and restoring a bundled config file now shows you the diff first, with
    every backup on disk offered as something to compare against and restore from.

    The patch digit again rather than a fourth part, on the same rule 0.9.6 used: two features
    rather than a fix. 0.9.7.0 rises above 0.9.6.0, which is what App Installer compares.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <VersionPrefix>0.9.8.0</VersionPrefix>
    <VersionSuffix>beta.12</VersionSuffix>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
